{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489327-updating-old-paths-to-the-new-sorcery-system","id":1489327,"title":"Updating Old Paths to the New Sorcery System","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-06T07:41:50-07:00","id":1489327,"title":"Updating Old Paths to the New Sorcery System","content":"So there are some paths that have no easy analogs in the Sorcerer book but that exist in the 20th-anniversary editions/prior editions and I started pondering how to alter them to fit with the casting system in M20 Sorcerer. I would like some advice/thoughts on how to update them.<br /> <br /> So far the paths that make sense to me are:<br /> <br /> Spirit Chasing(W20 Kinfolk)<br /> <br /> Ash Casting(Investigator's Handbook...like it is weirdly labeled as a psychic numen when it is clearly a form of grave ash magic thing)<br /> <br /> The Path of Dowsing(Liege, Lord, and Lackey)<br /> <br /> There are more of course but several of them I feel are already represented adequately by the existing paths like Summoning, Binding, Warding which covers a lot of the individual paths for summoning spirits and ghosts that the Society of Leopold and the Society of the Weeping Moon uses.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway...thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T09:25:32-07:00","id":1489341,"title":"","content":"Storyteller's Vault addresses a few of these. Sorcerer: Paths of Power has M20-compatible writeups for Chronomancy, Gauntlet Manipulation, Saturnal Anima/Manes (the Paths of the Society of the Weeping Moon), Spirit Awakening, and Spirit Chasing, as well as every Path in M20 Sorcerer except the ones from Ghost Hunters; Sorcerer's Companion has M20-compatible writeups for Dowsing, Spirit-Chasing, Chronomancy, and Illusion. <br /> <br /> In terms of Paths that don't have any M20 Sorcerer updates: <br /> <br /> The Dreamspeakers Revised Tradition provided Static Shamans with access to Spirit Command, Spirit Awakening, Gauntlet Manipulation, and Summon Naturae. S:PoP covers the Gauntlet Manipulation and Spirit Awakening; Spirit Command and Summon Naturae can largely be folded into Summoning/Binding/Warding. <i>Can</i> be, but don't <i>have to</i> be: one thing about Paths is that they <i>don't</i> originate from a systematic codification of what's possible with magic; they're frequently created ad hoc. <br /> <br /> The Theurgy Paths of the Society of Leopold all have equivalents in M20 Sorcerer: Via Medicamenti (Healing), Via Ignis (Hellfire? Or Pyromancy?), Via Geniorum (spirit-focused Summoning/Binding/Warding), Via Necromantiae (Mortal Necromancy? Or ghost-focused Summoning/Binding/Warding?), and Via Oraculi (Divination). <br /> <br /> (I wouldn't mind a V20 update of Inquisition; but the selling point to me would be to do it as a modernb-day version of Dark Ages: Inquisitor. But that's beyond the scope of this thread.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T09:43:48-07:00","id":1489346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489327-updating-old-paths-to-the-new-sorcery-system?p=1489341#post1489341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storyteller's Vault addresses a few of these. Sorcerer: Paths of Power has M20-compatible writeups for Chronomancy, Gauntlet Manipulation, Saturnal Anima/Manes (the Paths of the Society of the Weeping Moon), Spirit Awakening, and Spirit Chasing, as well as every Path in M20 Sorcerer except the ones from Ghost Hunters; Sorcerer's Companion has M20-compatible writeups for Dowsing, Spirit-Chasing, Chronomancy, and Illusion.<br /> <br /> In terms of Paths that don't have any M20 Sorcerer updates:<br /> <br /> The Dreamspeakers Revised Tradition provided Static Shamans with access to Spirit Command, Spirit Awakening, Gauntlet Manipulation, and Summon Naturae. S:PoP covers the Gauntlet Manipulation and Spirit Awakening; Spirit Command and Summon Naturae can largely be folded into Summoning/Binding/Warding. <i>Can</i> be, but don't <i>have to</i> be: one thing about Paths is that they <i>don't</i> originate from a systematic codification of what's possible with magic; they're frequently created ad hoc.<br /> <br /> The Theurgy Paths of the Society of Leopold all have equivalents in M20 Sorcerer: Via Medicamenti (Healing), Via Ignis (Hellfire? Or Pyromancy?), Via Geniorum (spirit-focused Summoning/Binding/Warding), Via Necromantiae (Mortal Necromancy? Or ghost-focused Summoning/Binding/Warding?), and Via Oraculi (Divination).<br /> <br /> (I wouldn't mind a V20 update of Inquisition; but the selling point to me would be to do it as a modernb-day version of Dark Ages: Inquisitor. But that's beyond the scope of this thread.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Love the DA Inq love...it is a hidden gem tbh. I don't remember off the top of my head, but how well does the Sorcerer paths to Power book match the new official M20 Sorcerer book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T10:31:30-07:00","id":1489350,"title":"","content":"Fairly well, overall. The author of Paths of Power was one of the writers for M20 Sorcerer; and my personal theory is that S20 Sorcerer bypassed so much of the usual development process because Paths of Power was used as a starting point for it. <br /> <br /> I haven't yet done a Path by Path comparison between the two; but where I have, I haven't found any substantial changes. Some presentation changes and some tightening up of the wording; but nothing that affects how they function. As well, most or all of the innovations I've found in M20 Sorcerer first appeared in Paths of Power. <br /> <br /> The main <i>differences</i> I'm finding are in the faction writeups, the most significant being that the Asatru Futhark (PoP) have been <i>wiped out</i> and replaced by the Forn Jafna\u00f0r (S20). I haven't looked too closely at the others yet; I generally go with solitary sorcerers myself. But I hear that S20 does more in terms of actual changes from previous source material than PoP does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}